---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { issuesUrl, statusNames } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout title="About & safety — OrcaBits">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About & safety</h1>
    <h2>A public place to discover plugins</h2>
    <p>
      This is a best-effort catalogue of OrcaSlicer plugins found on GitHub,
      maintained by an individual. It brings links together on an open website
      because Orca Cloud requires an account even to browse plugins. Browsing
      here needs no account; installation still uses the author's download or an
      Orca Cloud account.
    </p>
    <p>
      This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by OrcaSlicer, its
      development team, or Orca Cloud.
    </p>
    <h2>Listed does not mean tested or safe</h2>
    <p>
      Plugins are not tested, audited, or certified by this catalogue.
      Descriptions, status, and compatibility are based on their authors'
      declarations and public documentation. Information may be incomplete,
      incorrect, or out of date, and GitHub stars are not a safety rating.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plugins are code you run on your machine. Depending on their permissions,
      they may access files, credentials, networks, or printers. Review the
      source and requested permissions, keep backups, and inspect generated
      G-code before using it. Installation and use are at your own risk; this
      catalogue provides no warranty and accepts no responsibility for damage,
      data loss, or other consequences.
    </p>
    {
      issuesUrl && (
        <>
          <h2>Report suspicious or malicious plugins</h2>
          <p>
            If you find a suspected malicious plugin in this catalogue,{" "}
            <a href={issuesUrl}>open an issue in the catalogue repository</a>.
            Include the plugin link and supporting evidence, without sharing
            credentials or other private data.
          </p>
          <p>Do not run a plugin to prove that it is malicious.</p>
          <h2>Suggest a plugin</h2>
          <p>
            Know an OrcaSlicer plugin that is missing here?{" "}
            <a href={issuesUrl}>Open an issue to suggest it</a> and include a
            link to its repository.
          </p>
          <h2>Request removal</h2>
          <p>
            If you are a plugin author and do not want your plugin listed here,{" "}
            <a href={issuesUrl}>open an issue to request removal</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }
    <h2>How to read status</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>{statusNames.available}</dt><dd>
        The author documents a usable installation and workflow; this does not
        guarantee stability or active maintenance.
      </dd>
      <dt>{statusNames.experimental}</dt><dd>
        A preview, proof of concept, or installable plugin with material
        compatibility or testing uncertainty.
      </dd>
      <dt>{statusNames.deprecated}</dt><dd>
        The author explicitly discourages further use or identifies a
        replacement.
      </dd>
      <dt>{statusNames.archived}</dt><dd>
        The repository is archived; review whether it still works with your
        setup.
      </dd>
    </dl>
    <h2>Dates and GitHub statistics</h2>
    <p>
      “Data updated” shows when catalogue information or GitHub statistics last
      changed. Stars are snapshots, not live counters; an em dash means the
      count is unknown. Plugins sharing a repository also share its star count.
    </p>
    <h2>Is this page made with AI?</h2>
    <p>Yes.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
